# Zero-config mode
# No environment variables are required to open the Control Room or connect ChatGPT / Codex.
#
# GitHub uses OAuth Device Flow from the UI.
# No GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET or SESSION_SECRET is required.
#
# Optional bootstrap only:
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
#
# The GitHub Client ID is public (not a secret). If present, the app uses it automatically.
# If it is absent, the GitHub connect screen can ask for it once and remember it in a secure cookie.
#
# ChatGPT / Codex uses Sign in with ChatGPT through Codex device authorization.
# Codex credentials are kept in HttpOnly/Secure cookies and restored only into ephemeral Vercel Sandboxes.
# No OPENAI_API_KEY or ChatGPT token is required in Vercel.
